LOCK(1)                     User Commands

NAME
    lock - lock the graphical session

SYNOPSIS
    lock

DESCRIPTION
    lock locks the session of the display server X12 and covers the
    screen. While the session is locked, X12 shows only the lock screen
    and sends all input to it. The lock screen shows the account of the
    caller and a password field. The right password, checked by
    checkpass(1), unlocks the session, and lock exits.

    X12 starts lock for Super+L and after the idle time set on the
    Display page of the Settings application (the setting lock_timeout of
    /etc/desktop.conf in seconds, 0 for never). The Lock row of the power
    menu of the panel starts it as well.

    When lock ends without an unlock, the session remains locked, and X12
    shows a black screen. A key press then starts lock again.

EXIT STATUS
    0 after the unlock. 1 when X12 refuses the lock, for example while
    another instance of lock runs.

SEE ALSO
    checkpass(1), greeter(1)
